{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the beast you shall kill.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, explained: if a person sinned, what did the beast sin? Rather, because through it a stumbling block came to a person, therefore the Torah said it shall be stoned — a fortiori, all the more so for one who knows how to distinguish between good and evil and causes a stumbling block for his fellow to transgress. Of the same matter you find (Deuteronomy 12:2): ״אבד תאבדון את כל המקומות״ — a fortiori: if the trees, which do not see and do not hear, because through them a stumbling block came, the Torah said to destroy, burn, and consume — how much the more so one who leads his fellow astray."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:19.998126756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}